[Term]
id: PREFER:0000150
name: data acquisition mode
def: "How, where, and when process data or samples are collected and measured during a bioprocess. The modes included are inline, online, atline, and offline." [PREFER]

[Term]
id: PREFER:0000151
name: inline measurement
def: "The analyzer is integrated into the bioreactor and the measurement is taken continuosly into the bioreactor. The sample flows continuously through the analyzer. The measurament is real-time with high frequency data, enabling real-time process monitoring and control." [PREFER]
is_a: PREFER:0000150 ! data acquisition mode

[Term]
id: PREFER:0000152
name: online measurement
def: "Analysis method that extracts a sample from the bioreactor and introduces it into the measurement zone. Sample can either be discarded or returned to the bioreactor." [PREFER]
is_a: PREFER:0000150 ! data acquisition mode

[Term]
id: PREFER:0000153
name: atline measurement
def: "Analysis method that extracts a sample from the process line and transporte it to a nerby analyzer. There is delay between sampling and measurment." [PREFER]
is_a: PREFER:0000150 ! data acquisition mode

[Term]
id: PREFER:0000154
name: offline measurement
def: "Analysis method that collects a sample from the process line and transports it to the analyzis laboratory. The sample is not returned to the process line." [PREFER]
is_a: PREFER:0000150 ! data acquisition mode

[Term]
id: PREFER:0000155
name: performance variable
def: "Computed variables that assess bioprocess efficiency, suchas as yields, rates, respiratorymetrics, and balance metrics." [PREFER]

[Term]
id: PREFER:0000156
name: yield
def: "Computed variable that quantifies the efficiency of converting substrates into desired outputs, expressed as the ratio of the output formed per unit of substrate consumed." [PREFER]
is_a: PREFER:0000155 ! performance variable

[Term]
id: PREFER:0000157
name: rate
def: "Computed variable that quantifies the speed of bioprocess activities, measuring the change of a process variable over time." [PREFER]
is_a: PREFER:0000155 ! performance variable

[Term]
id: PREFER:0000158
name: respiratory metric
def: "Computed variable that quantifies respiratory activity in the bioprocess, providing indications of metabolic states and gas exchange efficiency." [PREFER]
comment: "For instance, oxygen uptake rate (OUR), carbon dioxide evolution rate (CER), respiratory quotient (RQ), and related metrics."
synonym: "metabolic metric" EXACT []
is_a: PREFER:0000155 ! performance variable

[Term]
id: PREFER:0000159
name: production metric
comment: "For instance, product yields, productivity rates"
is_a: PREFER:0000155 ! performance variable

[Term]
id: PREFER:0000160
name: growth metric
comment: "For instance, specific growth rate, biomass yields."

[Term]
id: PREFER:0000180
name: operational mode
def: "A defined strategy of operating a bioreactor that specifies how culture medium and biomass are introduced, maintained, and removed over time." [PREFER]

[Term]
id: PREFER:0000181
name: batch
def: "An operational mode in which all nutrients are supplied at the start of cultivation, with no further input or removal of medium until the end of the process." [PREFER]
synonym: "batch cell culture" EXACT [MSIO:0000181]
synonym: "batch culture" EXACT []
xref: MSIO:0000181
is_a: PREFER:0000180 ! operational mode

[Term]
id: PREFER:0000182
name: fed-batch
def: "An operational mode in which additional nutrients are intermittently or continuously supplied to the culture during cultivation, without removal of culture fluid, until termination of the process." [PREFER]
is_a: PREFER:0000180 ! operational mode

[Term]
id: PREFER:0000183
name: continuous-chemostat
def: "A continuous operational mode in which fresh medium is supplied and culture fluid removed at a constant rate, such that the specific growth rate of the biomass is controlled by the limiting nutrient concentration and equals the dilution rate." [PREFER]
is_a: PREFER:0000180 ! operational mode

[Term]
id: PREFER:0000184
name: continuous-turbidostat
def: "A continuous operational mode in which fresh medium is supplied and culture fluid removed in response to feedback control, such that the biomass concentration is maintained constant at a predefined turbidity or optical density." [PREFER]
is_a: PREFER:0000180 ! operational mode

[Term]
id: PREFER:0000185
name: bioreactor scale
def: "A classification of bioreactors based on culture volume and intended application, ranging from laboratory research to industrial production." [PREFER]

[Term]
id: PREFER:0000186
name: lab-scale
def: "A bioreactor scale typically used for small-scale experiments and research, ranging from a few milliliters to several liters in volume." [PREFER]
comment: "For instance, minibioreactors (50-500 mL) such as Ambr or Pioreactors, or micro bioreactors (< 10 mL) fall within this category." [PREFER]
is_a: PREFER:0000185 ! bioreactor scale

[Term]
id: PREFER:0000187
name: pilot-scale
def: "A bioreactor scale that serves as an intermediate step between lab-scale and industrial-scale, typically ranging from several liters to a few hundred liters in volume." [PREFER]
is_a: PREFER:0000185 ! bioreactor scale

[Term]
id: PREFER:0000188
name: industrial-scale
def: "A bioreactor scale used for large-scale production, typically ranging from several hundred liters to thousands of liters or more in volume." [PREFER]
is_a: PREFER:0000185 ! bioreactor scale

[Term]
id: PREFER:0000189
name: feed profile
def: "The feeding strategies typically found in a fed-batch fermentation type. The type of feeding profiles applied is process specific." [PREFER]
synonym: "feed stream profile" NARROW []
synonym: "feeding profile" EXACT []
synonym: "feeding strategy" EXACT []
relationship: refers_to_variable PREFER:0000037 ! feed

